{"id": "EUVD-2026-103624", "enisaUuid": "7f621313-e87a-3cf8-89f9-498daa5d014d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnfc: llcp: fix sdreq TLV list leak on parse/alloc/send failure\n\nnfc_genl_llc_sdreq() builds a list of TLV nodes while walking nested\nnetlink attrs, but 3 error paths (nested-attr parse failure, TLV alloc\nENOMEM, nfc_llcp_send_snl_sdreq() failure) all skip freeing what was\nalready queued.\n\nRoute them through a new free_list label, mirroring the SDRES path in\nthe same file which already does this. Harmless on the success path\ntoo -- send_snl_sdreq() drains the list as it moves nodes, so it's\nalready empty by the time free_list runs.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:18:52", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:22:04", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5b1eca82085134bd92cd3810b0ef003c91e3f668", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d3f60a7fc291d08cd9192a3b4cd5d3a223fa7d02", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/755bfc409748d8f3df64eb0eb26926270de3dd77", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e43ec0191c1630f41e7043ac729ea6f1b8044a7f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/08d2c069239ab425fdd333784a6a3b3e034e4aa0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cbde7f5d326172d6dbb55cca0df42fa7e1ed8115", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0b01a946b0f234f5badd25968610b585a4895f08", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/66f4300206b82b0b143ef0d9be90cd8d29f23a47"], "aliases": ["GHSA-g53r-f4w7-7x66", "CVE-2026-98579"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1a63b6d4-fcad-372a-a58e-256c7ee57cca", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d9b8d8e19b073096d3609bbd60f82148d128b555 <e43ec0191c1630f41e7043ac729ea6f1b8044a7f"}, {"id": "2ad68304-6d43-30a7-b55d-b42cd604196c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d9b8d8e19b073096d3609bbd60f82148d128b555 <755bfc409748d8f3df64eb0eb26926270de3dd77"}, {"id": "2d52ecd5-2afd-30fd-ad1c-